   {
    "name": "add_reminder",
    "description": "Record unfinished work in Docs/todos.md so a later session can pick it up.\nCall it the moment you:\n- leave a partial implementation (a stub, a skipped branch, a placeholder value),\n- hit a design question nobody has decided (a balance number, an unspecified edge case),\n- hear the user defer something (\"later\", \"not now\").\nDon't call it for every ponytail: comment; /ponytail-debt covers those.\npriority: P1 = something is broken or blocks other work, P2 = a feature is incomplete, P3 = polish or cleanup.\nat: optional repo-relative pointer to the partial code, e.g. src/api/orders.ts:42.\nWord the text by the reminders:writing-reminders skill; load it before your first reminder in a session.\nThe text must make sense with no context from this conversation."
   },
   {
    "name": "list_reminders",
    "description": "List open reminders from Docs/todos.md, sorted P1 to P3. Call only when the user asks about open work or reminders."
   },
   {
    "name": "complete_reminder",
    "description": "Mark an open reminder in Docs/todos.md done; it moves to the Done section.\nmatch: a case-insensitive piece of the reminder text that matches exactly one open item.\nIf the item's pointer leads to a TODO/FIXME/ponytail: comment or a TODO note in memory/, delete that marker in the same change."
   },
   {
    "name": "reopen_reminder",
    "description": "Move a reminder in Docs/todos.md from Done back to Open, keeping its priority and date.\nCall it when the user says an item was marked done by mistake, or the work turns out unfinished.\nmatch: a case-insensitive piece of the reminder text that matches exactly one Done item."
   }
